      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cnkv9iyo9cirxfnn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1250,
      "y": 340,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "text": "common ground to\nEACH galvo driver\n(and the ±15 V COM)",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cnkv9no9mcqn5r",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1250,
      "y": 670,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "text": "Do NOT ground IN−.\nThe drive is differential;\ngrounding it halves the\nrange and invalidates the\ncoordinate mapping.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "nz",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 850,
      "width": 1420,
      "height": 160,
      "backgroundColor": "#fff5f5",
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cnkv9w2caw4fr02s",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 58,
      "y": 862,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "text": "BEFORE CONNECTING THE DACs TO THE GALVO DRIVER — open no-go item (§10)",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cnkv93zspge9fb6u",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 58,
      "y": 892,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "text": "The two channels of an axis are complementary unipolar 0–5 V outputs, so the pair presents a permanent 2.5 V COMMON MODE. It is the operating point, not a transient.\n\"±5 V analog input at 0.33 V/°\" in a seller listing establishes none of the following. Confirm all three from the driver's own manual:\n     1.  IN+ / IN− are a genuine differential pair — not two single-ended inputs, and not one input with the other meant to be grounded.\n     2.  The permitted input common-mode range includes 2.5 V.\n     3.  The ±5 V figure is a DIFFERENTIAL rating, not ±5 V per input measured to ground.\nIf any is wrong, §14 and CoordinateMapper are wrong and every commanded angle carries a silent scale or offset error. Re-check empirically during calibration:\ncommand a known angle, measure the actual deflection. Do not resolve this by trial with any laser connected.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cnkv97hlc8c90s8j",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 1050,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "text": "/LDAC and /SHDN are not optional.  Both are CMOS inputs with no internal pull. With /LDAC floating HIGH the serial latch never transfers to the output:\nMCP4922::write() returns success, the SPI traffic scopes correctly, and the outputs never move. It is the most likely thing to cost you an evening at DAC bring-up.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cnkv9qd23s2wwvn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 1100,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "text": "MOSI and SCLK get no external bias, deliberately.  They cannot float while the buffer is powered — the 5 V logic rail comes from the Pi header, so the translator\nis energised only when the Pi is, and GPIO 9–27 default to internal pull-downs at reset. With /CS held HIGH by its pull-up, no write can latch regardless.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cnkv9e13ubbw7wud",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 1150,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "text": "Vref is the Pi's 5 V rail, valid only because the driver writes BUF = 0 (unbuffered, range 0..VDD).  dac_reference_voltage in system_config.yaml must hold the\nMEASURED rail voltage at the DAC pin under load, not 5.0 — CoordinateMapper divides by it, so 2 % error is 2 % of commanded angle: ~0.3° full scale, ≈4 mm at 0.75 m.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cnkv9zsxnavn1wef",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 1200,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "text": "For breadboard bring-up lower spi_speed_hz to about 1 MHz and scope MOSI/SCLK/CE0/CE1 AT THE MCP4922 PINS. One control cycle is four 16-bit transfers, so the\nclock is never the bottleneck, and 20 MHz edges on jumper wire will ring.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:07:14.283Z",
      "version": 1
    }
  ],
  "appState": {
    "viewBackgroundColor": "#ffffff",
    "gridSize": null
  }
}